# lahn course
version 1
title First steps
description Never held a bass? Start here. One string, then the next, then your first frets and the names of the notes: a little at a time, at your own pace.
instrument bass

unit Meet your bass

lesson Your very first note
title Four strings
text Your bass has four strings. The thickest one sounds the lowest, the thinnest one the highest.
text On lahn's neck the thinnest string is at the top, the thickest at the bottom, the way bass tab shows them.
title Open strings
text Playing a string "open" means you don't press anything on it: you just pluck it with a finger (or a pick).
text Pluck the thinnest string now: the G string. lahn lights it on the neck, and hears you when you play it.
text No sound reaching lahn? Check that your bass is plugged in, and the input in Settings.
exercise
type notes
places 4:0
show neck
count 3
pass 2

lesson The thickest string
text Now the other end: the thickest string, at the bottom of the neck. It's the E string, the lowest note of the bass.
exercise
type notes
places 1:0
show neck
count 3
pass 2

lesson Up and down the open strings
title E, A, D, G
text From the thickest to the thinnest, the open strings are E, A, D and G.
text To remember them: Eat All Day, Girl. Play them one after the other, then back.
exercise
type notes
places 1:0 2:0 3:0 4:0 3:0 2:0
show neck
order in_order
count 6
pass 5

lesson Any open string
text Now in any order: watch which string lights up.
exercise
type notes
places 1:0 2:0 3:0 4:0
show neck
count 8
pass 7

lesson Strings by name
text This time lahn says the string's name, and shows where it is. Play it open.
exercise
type notes
places 1:0 2:0 3:0 4:0
show name
where yes
count 8
pass 7

lesson Strings by name, no hints
text The same, without the neck showing you where. If you slip, lahn shows the right one.
exercise
type notes
places 1:0 2:0 3:0 4:0
show name
count 8
pass 7

unit Your first frets

lesson Pressing a fret
title Frets
text The metal bars across the neck are the frets. Pressing a string down just behind one makes it shorter, and the note higher.
text Press with the tip of your finger, close to the fret, firmly enough for the note to ring clean. Then pluck.
title Fret 2
text Press the G string at the 2nd fret with your first finger, and pluck it.
exercise
type notes
places 4:2
show neck
count 3
pass 2

lesson Fret 4
text Now the 4th fret, with your third or fourth finger: one finger a fret, your hand stays put.
exercise
type notes
places 4:4
show neck
count 3
pass 2

lesson Open, 2, 4
text The G string open, then fret 2, then fret 4, in any order.
exercise
type notes
places 4:0 4:2 4:4
show neck
count 8
pass 7

lesson On the D string
text The same on the next string down, the D string: open, fret 2, fret 3.
exercise
type notes
places 3:0 3:2 3:3
show neck
count 8
pass 7

lesson Two strings
text Both strings now, all six places. Watch which string lights up.
exercise
type notes
places 3:0 3:2 3:3 4:0 4:2 4:4
show neck
count 10
pass 8

unit The names of the notes

lesson G, A and B
title Every note has a name
text Notes are named with letters, A to G. The open G string is a G, its 2nd fret is A, its 4th fret is B.
text lahn says the name and shows where it is. Play it.
exercise
type notes
notes G2 A2 B2
show name
where yes
count 8
pass 7

lesson G, A and B, no hints
text Now just the name. A slip shows you where it was.
exercise
type notes
notes G2 A2 B2
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson D, E and F
text On the D string: open is D, fret 2 is E, fret 3 is F.
exercise
type notes
notes D2 E2 F2
show name
where yes
count 8
pass 7

lesson D, E and F, no hints
exercise
type notes
notes D2 E2 F2
show name
octave exact
count 8
pass 7

lesson Six notes
title From D to B
text D, E, F on the D string, then G, A, B on the G string: six notes in a row, the alphabet going on from one string to the next.
exercise
type notes
notes D2 E2 F2 G2 A2 B2
show name
octave exact
count 12
pass 10
title What next
text You can find twelve places and six notes by name. The Reading course writes these same notes on the staff; Neck walk, in Games, plays with them to music.
